-- title:
--   Theorem 12 — uniform deterministic flooding horizon
-- statement:
--   Assume that in every round the physical graph has $n$ vertices including the fixed Byzantine set, is $D$-regular, has normalized absolute spectral gap at least $\hat\lambda_0\in(0,1]$ and $\kappa(G_r)>2(t+c)$; $|B|\le t$; at most $c$ correct replacements per transition. Let $I_r\subseteq C_r$ be the correct holders of a report generated by correct $v$ in round $q$ (immediately before forwarding), with $v\in I_q$, and assume correct-to-correct forwarding of every retained report over every current edge with retention through the beginning of round $q+L_{\mathrm{flood}}$: for $q\le r<q+L_{\mathrm{flood}}$, a correct process of round $r+1$ that held the report in round $r$, or has a $G_r$-neighbour that held it, holds it in round $r+1$. Then every correct process present throughout $[q,q+L_{\mathrm{flood}}]$ holds the report at the beginning of round $q+L_{\mathrm{flood}}$, where $L_{\mathrm{flood}}=2\lceil4/\hat\lambda_0\rceil+\lceil6\ln n/\hat\lambda_0\rceil+\lceil4\ln n/\hat\lambda_0\rceil+4$. The guarantee is deterministic and holds for every (hence every adaptively chosen) topology and churn sequence.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: correct-to-correct forwarding of every retained report over every current incident edge in every round, and retention of the round-q report through the beginning of round q + L_flood → an arbitrary holder sequence I_r ⊆ C_r with v ∈ I_q that is closed, for q ≤ r < q + L_flood, under keeping (w ∈ I_r, w present in r+1) and receiving from a G_r-neighbour in I_r; reason: every actual retained-report forwarding execution satisfies this closure; allowing extra holders and omitting identity freshness only enlarges the domain and preserves every source instance
--   - encoding: has received by the beginning of round q + L_flood → belongs to I at round q + L_flood (holders are taken after the deliveries at the beginning of the round); reason: same instant of the round
--   - encoding: deterministic guarantee against adaptive topology and churn → universal quantification over network and holder sequences satisfying the round, churn and forwarding hypotheses; reason: every history-adaptive execution induces such sequences; there is no probabilistic independence premise
-- source:
--   Sengupta and Perrin (2026), Byzantine Partition Detection Under Churn, supplied 48-page artifact (venue metadata: STOC 2027 submission; citation basis published per source.meta.json; SHA-256 3f9994406f38c73927d0b5cc78d0dd05740de0f7d09e544b7b203eefe39cdb74), Theorem 12, p. 22 (PDF 22)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CharonChurn_Main_Network

namespace CharonChurn.Main

/-- Theorem 12 (Uniform deterministic flooding horizon), p. 22. Every round's graph is
`D`-regular with absolute gap at least `λ̂₀ ∈ (0, 1]` and `κ(G_r) > 2(t + c)`; the Byzantine set
has at most `t` members and is never churned; at most `c` replacements per transition. Let
`I r ⊆ C_r` be the correct holders of a report generated by correct `v` in round `q`
(immediately before forwarding) and assume correct-to-correct forwarding over every current
edge together with retention through the beginning of round `q + L_flood`: for
`q ≤ r < q + L_flood`, a correct process of round `r + 1` that held the report in round `r` or
has a `G_r`-neighbour that held it, holds it in round `r + 1`. Then every correct process
present throughout `[q, q + L_flood]` holds it at the beginning of round `q + L_flood`. -/
theorem theorem_12 (P : Params) (N : Network) (hlam : 0 < P.lam) (hlam1 : P.lam ≤ 1)
    (hround : ∀ r, RoundOK P N r) (hB : N.B.card ≤ P.t) (hchurn : ∀ r, ChurnOK P N r)
    (q v : ℕ) (hv : v ∈ correctSet N q) (I : ℕ → Finset ℕ)
    (hI : ∀ r, I r ⊆ correctSet N r) (hsrc : v ∈ I q)
    (hfwd : ∀ r, q ≤ r → r < q + Lflood P.n P.lam → ∀ w ∈ correctSet N (r + 1),
      (w ∈ I r ∨ ∃ u ∈ I r, (N.G r).Adj u w) → w ∈ I (r + 1)) :
    ∀ w, w ∉ N.B → (∀ m ∈ Finset.Icc q (q + Lflood P.n P.lam), w ∈ N.V m) →
      w ∈ I (q + Lflood P.n P.lam) := by sorry

end CharonChurn.Main
